------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web source reproduced)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources: none (pure presentational primitive, per prompt). Still bound through the
  P1/S8 state-holder seam (WidgetTipCardsSource -> WidgetTipCardsModel) so the leaf
  contract states are driven by one snapshot; no HTTP in the view. A web-style direct
  props initializer `WidgetTipCards(tips:maxTips:compact:emptyMessage:emptyIconSystemName:)`
  mirrors `<WidgetTipCards tips=… />` for embedding inside host widgets.
- Composition: the `space-y-2` column of cards; each card = optional SF Symbol +
  title + trailing impact Badge (web `Badge` -> shared TSBadge) + description
  (line-clamped to 2 in the compact layout, web `line-clamp-2`); ≥44pt touch target.
- Windowing: `limit = maxTips ?? (compact ? 1 : 3)`, `visible = tips.prefix(limit)`
  reproduced verbatim (WidgetTipWindow).
- Impact tone map reproduced verbatim (web `impactBadgeMap`): high->success,
  medium->warning, low->neutral; badge label = web `impactLabel ?? impact` (localized).
- States (all render): loading (skeleton cards), empty (web EmptyState -> TSEmptyState,
  message `emptyMessage ?? 'No recommendations'`), error (web QueryError -> TSQueryError +
  retry), data, and the P4 leaf freshness axis stale/offline (freshness banner + one-shot
  auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- i18n: all strings via the P1/S10 facade (table "WidgetTipCards", WidgetTipCards.strings)
  with web English fallbacks; no English literals in Swift. Keys: empty, title,
  loadingA11y, impact.{high,medium,low}, staleBanner, offlineBanner.
- Accessibility: each card is one combined VoiceOver element
  ("{title}, {impact}, {detail}"); badge hidden (spoken via the card); loading label;
  freshness banner combined; Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS); reduce-motion honored
  via shared TSFadeIn / TSSkeleton.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): WidgetTipCardsModel.start() emits view.opened with slug
  "WidgetTipCards" (OSLogWidgetTipCardsTelemetry; asserted by a spy in the tests).

